{"id": "EUVD-2026-102991", "enisaUuid": "7f288fdd-f497-340b-9d0b-a7811f7499f3", "description": "WebVella ERP through 1.8.8 contains an sql injection vulnerability that allows any authenticated user to inject SQL through WHERE-clause text literals in the EQL query API. Attackers can send crafted single-quoted literals to POST /api/v3/en_US/eql, escaping the unsanitized EqlBuilder SQL interpolation to read unauthorized entities, including user and role tables.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T13:40:04", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/webvella-erp-eql-text-literal-sql-injection", "https://github.com/WebVella/WebVella-ERP/blob/10315fe844198b8620494f716ed75410cd54bfe6/WebVella.Erp/Eql/EqlBuilder.Sql.cs#L580-L581", "https://github.com/WebVella/WebVella-ERP/blob/10315fe844198b8620494f716ed75410cd54bfe6/WebVella.Erp.Web/Controllers/WebApiController.cs#L64-L74", "https://www.nuget.org/packages/WebVella.Erp/1.8.8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/webvella-erp-through-1.8.8-sql-injection-via-eql-query-api"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111700", "GHSA-5hxh-2p25-4hxp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "91e31407-8c19-3fc1-9bf2-c13c94332e19", "product": {"name": "WebVella-ERP", "vendor": {"name": "WebVella"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.8.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "66c7f3d7-d612-392c-83d1-a94f83d6e4f7", "vendor": {"name": "WebVella"}}], "isExploited": false}